.SH NAME
datui\-views \- list or remove saved views
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBdatui views list\fR
\fBdatui views rm\fR \fINAME\fR
\fBdatui views clear\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
List or remove saved views.
.PP
A view is saved from the views list (\fBv\fR) at the table, and applied with \fB\-\-view NAME\fR or from that list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdatui views list\fR
List the saved views: name, what files they match, when last used.
.TP
\fBdatui views rm\fR
Remove one saved view by name.
.RS
.TP
\fINAME\fR

.RE
.TP
\fBdatui views clear\fR
Remove every saved view.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Set a config key for this run, as in the file: \-c display.\:row_numbers=true. Repeatable; a flag of the key's own still wins. \fBdatui config keys\fR lists them.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success: the session was quit (q, Ctrl+Q or Ctrl+C), or the command did what it was asked.
.TP
\fB1\fR
An error, printed to standard error: a PATH that is not there, a configuration file that cannot be used, nothing piped in for \-, or a command that failed (datui formats check on a spec with errors).
.TP
\fB2\fR
A usage error: an unknown option or command, or a value an option does not take.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDATUI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
The config directory, in place of the platform's (\fB~/.config/datui\fR on Linux). Saved views and format specs live there too.
.SH FILES
\fICONFIG\fR is \fB$DATUI_CONFIG_DIR\fR when it is set, else \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/datui\fR (\fB~/.config/datui\fR) on Linux, \fB~/Library/Application Support/datui\fR on macOS and \fB%APPDATA%\edatui\fR on Windows.
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR/config.toml
The config file: see datui-config(5). \fBdatui config path\fR prints the files read.
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR/catalog.toml
Your catalog, which Ctrl+D on the home screen adds to: see datui-catalog(1).
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR/catalogs/
More catalogs, one *.toml each, named by its file; examples.toml replaces the bundled one.
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR/views/
Saved views: see datui-views(1).
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR/formats/
Format specs and dictionaries, searched first: see datui-formats(7).
.SH EXAMPLES
The saved views: name, the files each matches, when last used.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
datui views list
.EE
.RE
